{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","description":"Answers to the two questions people ask most about sharpening kitchen knives.","headline":"Knife sharpening questions","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Every few months for home use, or when the knife stops cutting a tomato cleanly."},"name":"How often should I sharpen a kitchen knife?"},{"@type":"Question","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. A serrated knife needs a rod made for serrated edges."},"name":"Can I use a whetstone on a serrated knife?"}],"url":"https://www.sharpkitchen.blog/knife-sharpening-questions"}